A barbarian has nothing to fear from the early game.  He's overloaded
with strength, dexterity, and constitution.  His HP-per-level is higher
than every other class in the game.  He has poison resistance built in.  
He starts with a weapon that does gallons of damage, and his first
artifact gift (if you're desperate) does even more gallons and has a 50%
chance of being the same weapon type he started the game with.

In short, he's one of the few classes that can handle soldier ants
straight up in melee when he first starts seeing them -- possibly the
_only_ class that can do so.  Remind me again why he needs to be so
super-duper careful in the early game?

Valks in vanilla are better in the long run because of the +3 shield, 
the built-in Excalibur for the lawfuls, and the ludicrously good quest
artifact.  But the Barbarian is far from weak sauce; he's another
excellent class for new players to start with while they learn the ropes.

